<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Aziz Billah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">955–996 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as appointed by al-Aziz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">Al-Aziz</a> Billah was the fifth Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> and the first to begin his reign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, ruling from 975 to 996. He extended Fatimid power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and built up the army by recruiting Turkish and other troops alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> forces. His reign was a period of prosperity and the appointment of capable officials, including non-Muslims.</p></div>
